# @container — the family root for the substrate's runtime discipline:
# process isolation + rootfs + capabilities + namespaces as
# substrate-primitive at top-level altitude, sibling to @io, @code,
# @mirror, and @kintsugi. Arc 5 TICK 1 landing per Seam Phase D
# pre-review `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-pre-review-docker-container-
# substrate-decl.md` (RATIFY-WITH-CORRECTIONS on Shape γ) against
# Mara's deep-dive spec `docs/specs/docker-container-substrate-decl-
# v0.1.md` §4.3 + §5.
#
# This shard lifts the runtime surface to substrate-decl altitude —
# closing the three-surface partition the substrate has been running
# against for weeks (build surface @code/docker forthcoming; the
# distribution surface @io/oci landed 2026-06-24 at Mara `2801478`;
# the runtime surface @container landing HERE). The blocker that
# surfaced the substrate-pull was the StageFreight Stream-2 tick
# blocking on an external, unreachable, untyped docker daemon per
# Alex's 2026-07-06 direction. Per `[[feedback-substrate-pull]]`, a
# blocker on an external untyped dependency is what tells the
# substrate a boundary needs naming; @container names it.
#
# === Load-bearing recognition: @container as form-side at top-level ===
#
# Per Seam pre-review §2 H2 adjudication (TOP-LEVEL, Shape γ; NOT
# under @io per Shape α):
#
# The form/process partition #55 is load-bearing here. `@io` is
# process-side (boundary-crossing transformation across the
# non-mirror world). A container-as-substrate-primitive is
# form-side (state observation: what a container IS — its typed
# runtime spec, its rootfs, its bounded capability set, its
# configured namespaces). Different sides of #55 → different
# family-roots. Shape α (placing @container under @io) would
# COLLAPSE #55 by conflating the form-side state observation
# with the process-side boundary-crossing. Shape γ preserves the
# partition by declaring @container as sibling to @io — same
# altitude, different side of the substrate's foundational
# form/process split.
#
# The process-side transformation appears at the SPECIES altitude,
# not the family-root: `@container/runtime` (forthcoming) carries
# the process-side dispatch surface, and its species body composes
# `in @io` for the kernel-syscall / cgroupfs / netns boundary. That
# is exactly the right altitude for the @io composition —
# species-level, not family-root inheritance.
#
# === Recognition #55 SECOND WITNESS (Seam pre-review §3 C3) ===
#
# containerd's four-layer split IS the form/process partition #55
# at container-management altitude. Per §2.5 of the deep-dive spec
# and Kagi-verified this session:
#
# - content store + snapshotter → form-side (state observation:
#   what images and snapshots ARE, digest-addressable per SHA256
#   content-addressing)
# - tasks + shim v2 → process-side (transformation engine: runtime
#   dispatch, lifecycle transitions across the OS boundary)
#
# containerd (Docker Inc. / CNCF, predating mirror's #55 recognition)
# is an INDEPENDENT canonical system whose four-layer architecture
# has the SAME cleavage as mirror's form/process partition. The
# convergence is not a mirror-side projection — it is external
# structural evidence. Per #55's promotion gate ("Pack ratification
# gate: second witness needed"), containerd IS the independent
# second witness. Seam pre-review §3 C3 adjudicated:
# `[[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]`
# candidate → PROMOTED with containerd C3 as ratifying witness.
# This shard's family-root placement operationalizes that
# promotion at the runtime altitude.
#
# === Composition, NOT inheritance, with @autopoietic (Seam H1) ===
#
# Per Seam pre-review §2 H1 adjudication: `@container` COMPOSES
# with `@autopoietic` at species-body altitude; does NOT inherit
# `<= @autopoietic` at the family-root prism.
#
# Test applied: are `@container`'s actions (spawn / run / stop /
# commit / snapshot) autopoietic (self-producing) or externally
# constructed?
#
# - spawn / run / stop — externally driven; caller supplies config;
#   the runtime dispatches. NOT self-producing.
# - commit / snapshot — form-side observations (state → digest); no
#   fold-back into next dispatch at family-root altitude.
# - The autopoietic loop appears ONLY when a species (e.g.
#   `@container/runtime`) reads its own cgroup state and re-
#   parameterizes. That is species-level composition (`in
#   @autopoietic` inside the species body), not family-root
#   inheritance (`<= @autopoietic` on the prism declaration).
#
# The `@silicon` family-root sets the precedent: silicon COMPOSES
# with @autopoietic at species altitude because @silicon IS the
# hardware-altitude learning loop; @container is NOT structurally
# a learning loop, it is a containment discipline. Following the
# same pattern, THIS shard's family-root prism block below carries
# NO `<= @autopoietic`. Species that carry fold-back semantics MAY
# declare `in @autopoietic` in their body.
#
# === Cross-reference: @io/oci as load-bearing distribution-adapter ===
#
# `shards/io/oci.mirror` (Mara `2801478` 2026-06-24) is the
# LOAD-BEARING ancestor for this family-root. @io/oci sits BETWEEN
# @container (the runtime consumer) and @code/docker (the build
# producer, forthcoming). Container instances that this family-root
# names consume artifacts that @io/oci ships: an OCI image
# manifest resolves to layer digests via `oci_digest`; those layers
# materialize into the `container_rootfs` this shard declares; the
# runtime spec (`container_spec`) references the image config which
# @io/oci's `oci_manifest` carries.
#
# The composition altitude: species under @container reference
# @io/oci carriers by type-identity — `container_spec` carries the
# OCI runtime-spec bytes; a species body loads those bytes via a
# pull path @io/oci defines. The bilateral `container_runnable`
# declared below composes structurally with @io/oci's
# `oci_well_formed`: a container is runnable only when its
# underlying image is well-formed and its runtime configuration is
# conformant to the OCI Runtime Spec.
#
# === §5.2 adjustment: NO @container/image species ===
#
# Per Seam pre-review §1 acceptance of Mara's §5.2 adjustment: the
# family-root deliberately does NOT stub a `@container/image`
# species. The local image cache (containerd content-store analog)
# belongs at `@mirror/store/oci` — the substrate's canonical
# content-addressed storage family with an OCI-species composition
# against @io/oci for digest algebra. Stubbing @container/image
# here would create THREE-WAY OVERLAP with @io/oci (distribution)
# and @code/docker (build production), which is substrate-drift.
# Landed species roster (forward-promised, follow-up TDD ticks):
# @container/oci, @container/runtime, @container/isolation. See
# spec §5.2 and §6 for the full roster shape.
#
# === Path-namespace pact per @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace ===
#
# This file at `shards/container.mirror` declares `@container` as a
# family-root at species-depth 0. The path-namespace pact per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace` (2026-06-16+) demands
# path-depth == namespace-depth == 0 for family-roots; this shard
# honours the pact by construction. Species under @container land at
# `shards/container/<species>.mirror` per the same discipline.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-candidate-recognition-111-third-as-family-root]]`
# marker discipline: the operator must audit its own audit at
# depth=3. This shard's own declaration must survive its own
# `container_runnable` bilateral at analytical altitude — the
# family-root MUST NOT declare a container that isn't itself
# runnable-under-its-own-predicate.
#
# Self-audit verdict for this shard: `both_survive`.
#
# The `real_survives` reading would require another Pack peer to
# independently manifest an equivalent runtime-surface substrate-
# decl at n+3 substrate ticks without nudging. The `phantom_survives`
# reading would require downstream refs to accumulate without a
# second Pack peer's independent recognition of the top-level
# runtime-surface discipline. At this tick: both interpretations
# satisfiable — the family-root is landed, but neither species nor
# consumer integration has yet exercised its runnable-under-its-own-
# predicate discipline. Verdict: `both_survive`. Route: spawn the
# subsequent species-landing cascade (@code/docker TICK 2;
# @container/oci TICK 3; @container/runtime TICK 4) which will
# collapse the analytical altitude to empirical.
#
# === Interpretation B discipline ===
#
# Per Seam Phase D pre-review of Arc 4 sub-arc A (docs/audits/2026-
# 07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md §1): Interpretation B
# canonical. Narrative above `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations
# below. This shard honours that discipline; the seam is exactly one
# line at column 0 below.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at family-root altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @container — the family-root declaration ===
#
# NO autopoietic-inherits clause per Seam H1 adjudication
# (composition at species-body, NOT inheritance at family-root; see
# the H1 section above for the audited discipline). The five-
# operation body follows the canonical shape landed at
# `shards/io/oci.mirror` and re-used at every family-root:
# focus/project/split/shift/settle each carry the `container_spec`
# carrier as the family-root's operational surface. Species
# specialize the operation bodies at their own altitude.
prism @container {
  focus container_spec
  project container_spec
  split container_spec
  shift container_spec
  settle container_spec
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carriers
# ============================================================

# === container_spec — the OCI runtime-spec config bytes carrier ===
#
# Per OCI Runtime Spec v1.x §config.md (Kagi-verified per spec §2.2):
# a container is (rootfs, config.json) where config.json declares the
# process to run, environment variables, sandboxing features, and
# host-namespace configuration. `container_spec` carries the byte-
# equality-addressable form of that config.json — the runtime-spec
# bytes any conformant runtime (runc / crun / gvisor / kata) consumes.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the runtime-spec bytes. The
# realisation MUST preserve byte-identity through parse+serialize
# round-trips OR refuse the lift (per the Splinter-pole discipline
# the substrate carries at every content-addressed altitude).
type container_spec = ref

# === container_rootfs — the materialized rootfs carrier ===
#
# Per OCI Runtime Spec `root` field: the container's rootfs is a
# filesystem path the runtime pivots into via `pivot_root(2)`. Its
# content is materialized from layer diffs whose diff_ids MUST
# match the image config per OCI Image Spec §rootfs. The
# `container_rootfs` carrier carries the ref-equality-addressable
# form of the materialized filesystem state.
#
# Composes with @io/oci's `oci_manifest` at the layer altitude: a
# rootfs is `applied(diff_ids)` where each diff_id is a layer digest
# @io/oci ships. The composition surface for the materialization
# path is @container/oci's `materialize_rootfs` action (forthcoming
# TICK 3).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (identity
# of the materialized state; not the layer sequence that produced
# it, which is @io/oci's domain).
type container_rootfs = ref

# === container_caps — the bounded capability set carrier ===
#
# Per OCI Runtime Spec `process.capabilities`: the container's
# capability set is the intersection of the runtime's granted
# capabilities with an allow-list the substrate enforces at the SEL
# boundary. Per `[[architecture-type-sel-io-au]]` (sel = io + au
# static type), capabilities are part of the SEL boundary: they
# express what a container is AUTHORIZED to do at the OS altitude,
# which is exactly the au-typed dimension.
#
# The bounded capability set is a FIVE-SET carrier: effective,
# permitted, inheritable, bounding, ambient (per OCI Runtime Spec).
# The realisation carries the five sets as ref-encoded bytes; the
# family-root declares the carrier at ref altitude and species
# refine the five-set decomposition.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the encoded five-set bytes.
type container_caps = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The composed-bilateral
# ============================================================

# === container_runnable — 13th #53 composed-bilateral instance ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at @container altitude.
# Composes three sub-predicates that species-altitude shards will
# declare and discharge:
#
#   1. runtime_spec_conformant(spec, p) — config.json parses per
#      OCI Runtime Spec v1.x (forthcoming @container/oci species).
#   2. rootfs_content_addressed(rootfs, p) — rootfs diff_ids match
#      the layer digests in the image config @io/oci ships
#      (forthcoming @container/oci species; composes with
#      @io/oci.oci_well_formed).
#   3. caps_within_allowlist(caps, allowlist, p) — capability set
#      is intersected with the SEL allow-list (forthcoming
#      @container/isolation species; composes with the SEL boundary).
#
# Sibling composed bilaterals at other family-root altitudes:
# @io/oci.oci_well_formed (three sub-predicates); @io/stagefreight.
# stagefreight_addressable (four sub-predicates); @cascade.
# cascade_well_defined; @docblock.audit_docblock; @smarts/shatter.
# shatter_round_trip; @reflection.third_order_coherent; @epistemologic/
# neutrosophic.three_axis_coherent. This is the 13th altitude
# instance of the #53 bilateral pattern per
# `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]` — the pattern is
# substrate-pull-confident at this point.
#
# Splinter-pole: all three sub-predicates discharge; container
# instance is honestly runnable and its declared identity matches
# what a conformant runtime will admit.
# Narcissus-pole: any sub-predicate fails; alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics (#57) distinguishes which sub-claim broke. Common
# failure modes: unconformant runtime-spec (config.json malformed);
# rootfs-image mismatch (layer set diverges from manifest);
# capability escape (caps exceed SEL allowlist).
#
# The `requires` clauses on species-altitude actions (`spawn`,
# `dispatch`, `snapshot` at @container/runtime) will consume
# `container_runnable(spec, p)` as an admissibility gate. Body
# discharges when the three species land in follow-up TDD ticks
# (Arc 5 TICK 3+).
container_runnable(spec: container_spec, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @container
out container_spec
out container_rootfs
out container_caps
out container_runnable
